UID:state-pte-rhode-island-2025-03-17@ustaxcalendar.com
DTSTAMP:20260924T122623Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250318
SUMMARY:Rhode Island: RI-1065 (partnership) / RI-1120S (S-corp) due
DESCRIPTION:Rhode Island partnership return due the 15th day of the 3rd mon
 th after year-end. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source stat
 es the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026
 -specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent wit
 h every other state in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shi
 ft policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, O
 regon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universa
 l US government-deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, 
 this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to M
 arch 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the general shift convent
 ion\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this spec
 ific state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Rhode Island
  partnership return due the 15th day of the 3rd month after year-end. Autom
 atic 6-month extension via Form RI-7004\, provided full estimated tax is pa
 id by the payment deadline. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited so
 urce states the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing
  the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consi
 stent with every other state in this data set that explicitly confirms a we
 ekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Mo
 ntana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near
 -universal US government-deadline convention of shifting to the next busine
 ss day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 
 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the general shif
 t convention\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that 
 this specific state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Aut
 hority: Rhode Island Division of Taxation\, direct fetch this session: "For
 m RI-1065 is due on or before the fifteenth day of the third month followin
 g the close of the taxable year" and "Automatic six (6) month extension for
  filers of... Form RI1120S or Form RI-1065." | Source: https://tax.ri.gov/s
 ites/g/files/xkgbur541/files/2026-01/2025%20RI-1065%20Instructions.pdf | Th
 is date is computed from a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-anno
